      "math_academy_id": "q-130958",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $D,$ given by\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $D$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $D$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$",
